  "notes": "Adecoagro NYSE-listed since Jan 2011 (IPO ticker AGRO). USD reporting; calendar fiscal year. Three operating segments: Sugar/Ethanol/Energy (S&EE), Farming (Crops + Rice + Dairy), and Land Transformation (farm sales). IFRS reporter — owned farms carried at fair value via biological assets / PP&E revaluation. Annual Cushman & Wakefield independent appraisal of land portfolio with Sep base date. Quarterly data sourced from 6-K earnings releases on adecoagro.com/Investor and SEC EDGAR (CIK 0001488934, 20-F filer). Adjusted EBITDA is the headline KPI in management releases. Net debt reported per company. El Meridiano farm sale closed Q4 2023 for $90M (Argentina). Hectare-to-acre conversion: 1 ha = 2.47105 acres. Land Transformation segment revenue is lumpy (depends on farm dispositions in any quarter). Some 2020-2022 quarterly granularity is approximate as company restated several segments under new IFRS 16 / biological asset standards. Quarterly expensesBySegmentMM are estimated by allocating annual COGS/SG&A/D&A pro-rata to revenue (annual totals tie to filings). Adecoagro does not disclose grossRevenueMM (US-style filer reports net revenue only). FY2011-FY2019 backfill from 20-F annual filings on EDGAR (CIK 0001488934) — annual only as quarterly archives are sparse pre-2020. IPO Jan-2011 raised $400M @ $11/share; ~117M shares outstanding post-IPO. Land portfolio peaked at ~285k ha (~705k acres) in 2014-2015 then steadily reduced via farm dispositions. Sugar/Ethanol segment expanded materially via Angélica + Ivinhema mill ramps (2011-2014).",
